> every time i launch the app, i have to manually set all my options
> (pickup types, text sizes, etc). i thought i would be able to copy the
> nethack defaults file over, edit it, and then copy it back and
> overwrite the original, but upon opening the copied one i seem to not
> have entries for things the options menu in program lets me alter (for
> example, the various window and menu font sizes).
>
> is there a way to set the options and then save an updated
> "defaults.nh" in game?

I used to just stick with the defaults, so even when I've been playing
the PPC version for a while I never thought about that.

I checked the defaults.nh file, indeed there are no lines concerning
the status text size. So I compared it to the PC version.

I added the following lines copied from PC version to the PPC version
(changed the values a bit too):

# Status window settings
OPTIONS=font_status:Tahoma,font_size_status:8

And it does work. The porting team decided to skip some lines to save
space, I guess. :)



